    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d414">

                <pb facs="0337" n="325" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg325"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.Consultation(2)/446</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Acting Secretary
                            of State to the Chief of the Division of the American
                        Republics</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Duggan</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-11">July 11, 1940</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Duggan</hi>: I think the suggestion contained in
                    the first paragraph on page 2 of Professor Fenwick’s letter<anchor n="99"
                        xml:id="d414-f1"/> deserves very serious consideration. I do not, however,
                    favor in the slightest degree the suggested resolution enclosed with his
                    letter.</p>
                <p>Please be kind enough to have drafted for my signature some appropriate
                    reply.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
